meta {
  name: Vol-ST Backtest
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/options/vol-st/backtest
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~underlying: AAPL
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Option ST Alert — Dry-Run Backtest

  Dry-run of the option-vol-st Supertrend alert WITHOUT delivery. For each underlying it loads
  the near-the-money contracts (both CALL and PUT) off the current stock price and evaluates
  every contract's legs — reporting the metrics and whether each qualifies ("what would fire
  right now"). Pure ST-driven: no ORB, no side gate, no latch.

  ## Legs (all on the option's own `timeframe`, default M1)
  - ST UP + rising: Supertrend direction UP and the line rising for `st-rising-candles` bars.
  - Above EMA: option close >= its `ema-period`-EMA on each of the last `ema-above-candles` bars
    (candle colour irrelevant).
  - Volume (optional, `volume-enabled`): session volume >= `min-session-volume` AND rising
    (recent-half avg > older-half avg over `volume-lookback`).
  Only ST-up contracts can qualify; non-ST-up contracts are still listed (stDirectionUp=false).

  ## Query
  - `underlying` — optional; scope to one symbol (e.g. AAPL). Omit for all configured.

  ## Response (200)
  {
    timeframe, stRisingCandles, emaPeriod, emaAboveCandles, volumeEnabled,
    minSessionVolume, volumeLookback, totalQualifying,
    results: [ { underlying, spot, contractsEvaluated, stUpContracts, qualifying,
                 contracts: [ { occSymbol, type, strike, moneyness, barsUsed,
                                stDirectionUp, stRising, stRisingStreak, aboveEma,
                                volumeOk, sessionVolume, recentAvgVol, olderAvgVol,
                                qualifies, note? } ] } ]
  }

  ## Notes
  - Options have no deep history via the API (most-recent-N only), so this is a LIVE dry-run
    reflecting the latest bar boundary — not a historical replay.
}
